WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.503
-President Trump held another
surreal press conference today

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.038
to defend
his Supreme Court nominee

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:09.242
after a last-minute Senate deal
to allow an FBI investigation.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.577
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:16.382
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:18.284
President Trump
is obviously very eager

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:21.287
to talk about anything other
than his historically unpopular

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.322
Supreme Court nominee,
Brett Kavanaugh.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:26.960
Only 35% of Americans believe
Kavanaugh's telling the truth,

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.562
and only 34%
support his nomination.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.765
And during the hearing,
it looked like he had

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:35.034
only about 33% support
from his wife.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:37.470
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.173
Although it doesn't surprise me
that this guy is unpopular.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.740
[ Laughter ]
I mean, look at him.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.310
He looks like the kind of guy
who yells at 6-year-olds,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.146
"You have to have a permit
for this lemonade stand!"

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:52.785
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:56.656
And today, Trump held another
surreal press conference

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.557
in the rose garden,
ostensibly to discuss

00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:00.893
his renegotiated NAFTA deal
with Mexico and Canada,

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.930
but as multiple female reporters
tried to ask him

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.664
about Kavanaugh,
he shot them down

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:08.267
in super demeaning
and sexist ways.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.603
-Yes, behind you, please.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.871
-Thank you, Mr. President.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.107
Now that you've answered
several questions on trade,

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.209
I'd like to turn --
-Don't do that. Don't do --

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.610
-Mr. President --
-Excuse me.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.811
Do you have a question on trade?

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.112
We'll do one or two
more questions on trade.

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:21.213
-You answered several questions
on trade --

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:22.648
-Okay, don't do that.
That's not nice.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:24.050
And besides that,
somebody is before you.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.487
Excuse me. Don't do that.
Do you have a question on trade?

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.587
-You answered
several questions on trade.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.089
-Do you have a question
on trade?

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.257
-My question
is on Judge Kavanaugh.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.525
-Okay, please, yes.
Go ahead, please, sir.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.393
-Just to wrap up...
-You know what?

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.629
You've really had enough.
Hey, you've had enough.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.398
Question?
Yeah, go ahead.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:41.100
Sure.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.335
She's shocked that I picked her.

00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:45.137
She's in a state of shock.

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:46.306
-I'm not.
Thank you, Mr. President.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.507
-That's okay.
I know you're not thinking.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.908
You never do.
-I'm sorry?

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:51.610
-No, go ahead.
Go ahead.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:55.948
-I mean, how much of a sexist
dick can you possibly be?

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.050
It's almost like --
Wait. Wait.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.586
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.590
It's almost like he saw
someone else getting attention

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:07.360
for acting like a maniac on TV
and thought, "I could top that."

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.428
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.428 --> 00:02:12.065
Trump offered a lengthy,
rambling defense of Kavanaugh,

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.400
and then he questioned the
credibility of one of the women

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.836
accusing Kavanaugh
of sexual assault.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.472
-Just to be clear,
should the FBI interview

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:23.176
all three
of Brett Kavanaugh's accusers?

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.077
-It wouldn't bother me at all.
Now, it depends.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:27.012
I don't know all three
of the accusers.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:30.082
Certainly, I imagine
they're going to interview two.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:32.551
The third one
I don't know much about,

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:34.486
but it wouldn't
bother me at all.

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:39.325
I mean, I've heard
that the third one has --

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.427
I have no idea
if this is true --

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.295
has very little credibility.

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:47.833
-Only Trump could say, "I have
no idea if this is true,"

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.868
and then question
whether someone else

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.171
is telling the truth.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:57.310
"I heard a rumor
she likes to spread rumors.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.611
Pass it on."

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:01.013
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:05.584
Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:08.587
...Trump was asked
about the FBI investigation

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.056
into the claims
against Kavanaugh

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.925
and whether that investigation
should include what seems like

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:15.961
some pretty obvious lies
about his heavy-drinking past.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:18.096
Trump again veered off
into a random tangent

00:03:18.096 --> 00:03:21.067
about the fact that he
doesn't drink alcohol at all.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.802
-But if he did lie
about his drinking,

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.069
does that mean
you'll pull his nomination?

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:25.671
-I don't think he did.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:29.408
Look, I'm just saying,
I'm not a drinker.

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:32.545
I can honestly say I never had
a beer in my life, okay?

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.645
-Right.

00:03:33.645 --> 00:03:35.882
-It's one of my
only good traits.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.349
I don't drink.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:38.651
Whenever they're
looking for something,

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.319
I say,
"Never had a glass of alcohol."

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:43.656
I've never had alcohol.
You know, for whatever reason.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.593
Can you imagine if I had
what a mess I'd be?

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.560
Would I be --
I'd be the world's worst.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.964
-What's amazing about that joke

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.832
is that,
inherent in the premise

00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:56.602
is Trump admitting
that he already sucks.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.170
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.305
I mean, think about it.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.807
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:06.045
That joke --
That joke doesn't work

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.947
if everyone thinks Trump
is a great president.

00:04:08.947 --> 00:04:11.650
He's basically saying, "If you
think I'm an [bleep] now,

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.319
imagine if I had a few beers."

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:18.624
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:21.794
"I'd be a [bleep] nightmare."

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.096
But Trump had a brief flicker
of self-awareness there,

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.766
and then it immediately vanished
as he complained again

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.167
about being treated unfairly
by the press.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:32.905
-I think the press has treated
me unbelievably unfairly.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.907
In fact, when I won,
I said, "The good thing is,

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.009
now the press finally gets it.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:39.845
Now they'll finally
treat me fairly."

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:41.814
They got worse.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.949
They're worse now than ever.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:46.085
They're loco, but that's okay.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:49.154
-I know Trump has never
had a beer in his life,

00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:51.757
but he talks like a guy
begging the bartender

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.393
to give him back his keys.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:57.429
"I can drive.

00:04:57.429 --> 00:04:59.331
You're being loco."

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:01.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.003
"Why?
He's being loco."

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:10.443
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.645
Trump's blood-alcohol level
could be zero,

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.513
and the bartender
would still say to him...

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:15.581
-You've had enough.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:18.918
-In fact,
much like a drunk guy at a bar

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.719
who starts telling his buddies
how much he loves them,

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:22.188
Trump decided
to get very personal

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.823
at a rally on Saturday
in West Virginia,

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.624
where he offered
this bizarre praise

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:27.893
for North Korean dictator
Kim Jong-un.

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:30.329
-I was really being tough,
and so was he.

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:32.564
And we would go back and forth.

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:35.134
And then we fell in love, okay?

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:38.037
No, really.
He wrote me beautiful letters.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:40.406
And they're great letters.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:41.874
We fell in love.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:45.644
-Man, if you'd told me
I would live to witness

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:49.348
a Republican President
telling a crowd in West Virginia

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:53.118
that he was in love
with a North Korean dictator,

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:55.187
I would've said,
"I'm sorry, buddy.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:57.456
I don't have a dollar,
and this my stop."

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:59.291
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:01.193
Also, I feel like...

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:04.596
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:04.596 --> 00:06:06.632
I really do feel like
it's worth pointing out

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:08.734
that when Trump
first got that beautiful letter

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.068
from Kim earlier this year,

00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:12.605
he admitted
that he hadn't even read it.

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:16.275
-A letter was given to me
by Kim Jong-un,

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:19.178
and that letter was
a very nice letter.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.381
Oh, would you like to see
what was in that letter.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.485
It was
a very interesting letter.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.656
-No, I didn't.
I haven't seen the letter yet.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.825
I purposely
didn't open the letter.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:34.726
-Oh, no, dude.

00:06:34.726 --> 00:06:37.263
Dude, you didn't
read the letter?

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.064
Before you talk about
how in love you are,

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:40.866
you might want
to read the letter.

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:43.803
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:46.439
But that's the thing.
The thing is...

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:48.540
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.976
...Trump would much rather
talk about his bromance

00:06:50.976 --> 00:06:53.078
with Kim Jong-un
than Republicans' handling

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:55.181
of the sexual-assault
allegations against Kavanaugh.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:58.750
For weeks, Democrats called
for a routine FBI investigation

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.286
which Republicans refused,
but then, on Friday,

00:07:01.286 --> 00:07:03.922
something dramatic
and unprecedented happened.

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:06.091
Arizona Senator Jeff Flake
announced that he would

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:08.060
vote "yes"
on Kavanaugh's confirmation,

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.795
and shortly after
he made that announcement,

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:12.164
he was confronted in an elevator
in the Capitol

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:13.966
by survivors of sexual assault,

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.101
courageously explaining their
own personal traumas

00:07:16.101 --> 00:07:19.005
and demanding that he explain
his vote to their faces.

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:21.240
Now, Flake was still
a "yes" on Kavanaugh,

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.843
but then, during the committee
hearing a few hours later,

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:26.812
Democratic Senator Chris Coons
floated a proposal

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:29.648
for a brief delay to allow
for an FBI investigation,

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:32.418
and then he and Flake
disappeared into a back room

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.086
while a bunch of other
Republican Senators

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:36.054
had no idea
what was happening.

00:07:36.054 --> 00:07:39.559
-After Democratic Senator Coons
floated his compromise,

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:42.995
Republican Jeff Flake
stood up and walked

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:46.732
from the Republican side
of the dais to the Democratic.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.501
-It all started
with this scene right,

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.069
Senator Flake
tapping his colleague

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.504
Chris Coons on the shoulder.

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:55.808
-Apparently, at some point
during the course of events,

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:58.744
something came,
up and he left the room.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:07:59.945
Something is happening.

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:01.213
We don't know what it is

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:03.382
or what it's going
to end up resulting in.

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:06.318
-And then, the room went silent,
and no one is saying anything,

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:10.556
and you could watch
the grim faces of Lindsey Graham

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:13.325
and Orrin Hatch and
Chuck Grassley sitting there,

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:15.127
helpless,
doing absolutely nothing.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:19.164
-Yeah, sure, but are those guys'
faces ever not grim?

00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:21.133
[ Laughter ]
I mean, look at them.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:24.637
They all look like they just got
the wrong order at the deli.

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:26.104
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.104 --> 00:08:27.673
They always look like
they're browsing

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:29.942
the Acorn Stairlift showroom.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:32.044
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:33.979
This looks like that movie
where some old guys

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:36.248
want to rob a bank
before they die.

00:08:36.248 --> 00:08:38.083
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:40.353
You just need --
Oh, there you go, there you go.

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:41.586
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.586 --> 00:08:42.888
I'd watch that On Demand.

00:08:42.888 --> 00:08:44.356
[ Applause ]

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:49.261
So, Flake went into a back room
and struck a deal with Democrats

00:08:49.261 --> 00:08:51.330
for a one-week delay
in the Kavanaugh vote

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.998
to allow
for an FBI investigation.

00:08:52.998 --> 00:08:54.166
When he came back out,

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.168
he tried to explain the deal
to everyone else.

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:58.103
There were still a lot of
details that were unclear.

00:08:58.103 --> 00:08:59.939
Would there actually be
a vote on Flake's proposal?

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:02.942
What exactly would a sufficient
investigation entail?

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:05.110
Instead, the chairman of the
committee, Chuck Grassley,

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:08.514
abruptly shut down the meetings,
citing an obscure rule.

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:10.916
And on a hot mic, you can hear
the other Senators

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:13.185
trying to figure out
what the hell just happened.

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:16.589
-I'm prepared to do it, make
a request to the White House,

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:19.892
to ask the FBI
to do that investigation.

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:23.462
It would be short
and limited in scope,

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.664
to the current allegations
that have been made.

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:28.601
-Mr. Chairman --
-But I would just encourage

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:30.902
the Democrats
who we talked to before

00:09:30.902 --> 00:09:35.607
to endorse that kind of thing,
that we can then move on.

00:09:35.607 --> 00:09:36.842
-Mr. Chairman.

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:39.545
-Because of the two-hour rule,
we're adjourned.

00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:56.462
-Oh, my God.

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:58.163
It's like watching
your grandparents

00:09:58.163 --> 00:10:00.066
try to operate a parking meter.

00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:01.967
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.967 --> 00:10:03.335
-"Did we get here at noon?

00:10:03.335 --> 00:10:05.137
When do we have
to put more money in?

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:07.305
It's two hours.
It's a two-hour rule."

00:10:07.305 --> 00:10:09.274
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:09.274 --> 00:10:12.178
"The two-hour rule.
I told you when we parked it."

00:10:12.178 --> 00:10:16.515
[ Applause ]

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:18.116
So, the basic outline
of the agreement

00:10:18.116 --> 00:10:20.586
was a one-week delay to allow
for an FBI investigation.

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:22.888
Afterwards, South Carolina
Senator Lindsey Graham

00:10:22.888 --> 00:10:25.391
was asked what had happened,
said he wasn't sure.

00:10:25.391 --> 00:10:26.525
But he did know one thing --

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:28.527
someone would have
to tell the President.

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:32.131
-What Jeff is saying is,
in the -- is --

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:33.832
makes sense to me.

00:10:33.832 --> 00:10:35.367
-Do you think that Murkowski --

00:10:35.367 --> 00:10:37.803
-I don't know.
I'm not speaking for Mitch.

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:40.339
I'm just --
I'm gonna talk with Jeff.

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:42.207
And somebody's
got to explain this to Trump,

00:10:42.207 --> 00:10:44.576
so I guess that'll be my job.

00:10:44.576 --> 00:10:46.779
-Oh, yeah.

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:49.548
Act like you hate it,
Br'er Rabbit.

00:10:49.548 --> 00:10:50.783
[ Laughter ]

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:53.385
"Somebody's
got to judge this pie contest.

00:10:53.385 --> 00:10:56.121
I guess I'll have to do it."
[ Laughter ]

00:10:56.121 --> 00:10:58.724
You love
being the Trump whisperer,

00:10:58.724 --> 00:11:01.560
because it keeps you on
the Sunday-morning talk shows.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.795
If it wasn't for Trump,
the only show you'd be on

00:11:03.795 --> 00:11:06.631
is the Food Network's
"Biscuits for One with Lindsey."

00:11:06.631 --> 00:11:11.970
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.173
"Welcome back.

00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:16.809
Tonight's guest is no one."

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:24.216
[ Laughter ]

00:11:24.216 --> 00:11:26.418
"Just me and you, biscuit."

00:11:26.418 --> 00:11:28.787
[ Laughter ]

00:11:28.787 --> 00:11:31.556
But then, as we learned more
about the FBI investigation,

00:11:31.556 --> 00:11:33.492
the less serious it seems.

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:34.960
It was reported that
the White House

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.196
had put strict limits
on who the FBI could talk to

00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:38.697
and what they could investigate.

00:11:38.697 --> 00:11:41.399
-In fact, the central figures
involved in the alleged assault

00:11:41.399 --> 00:11:43.201
weren't even on
the witness list.

00:11:43.201 --> 00:11:45.337
-"The New York Times" reports
that the White House

00:11:45.337 --> 00:11:48.941
authorized the FBI to interview
just four witnesses.

00:11:48.941 --> 00:11:53.712
-The FBI will question a
specific witness list this week,

00:11:53.712 --> 00:11:57.616
a list that does not include
Kavanaugh's third accuser,

00:11:57.616 --> 00:12:00.886
Julie Swetnick,
or former classmates

00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:03.488
who could share details
about Kavanaugh's

00:12:03.488 --> 00:12:06.559
college drinking habits
and shed, potentially,

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:09.028
some light on alleged
sexual references

00:12:09.028 --> 00:12:10.596
in his high school yearbook.

00:12:10.596 --> 00:12:13.398
-Sources telling CNN
Christine Blasey Ford

00:12:13.398 --> 00:12:15.500
and Supreme Court nominee
Brett Kavanaugh

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:19.472
are not on the initial list
given to the FBI

00:12:19.472 --> 00:12:21.840
suggesting who
they should interview.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:25.211
-Okay, if you start out
an investigation by listing

00:12:25.211 --> 00:12:27.313
all the things
you're not investigating,

00:12:27.313 --> 00:12:29.181
that's not a real investigation.

00:12:29.181 --> 00:12:31.483
That's like going
on a trip to Paris

00:12:31.483 --> 00:12:33.552
and saying, "I don't want
to see Eiffel Tower,

00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:35.020
the Louvre, or Notre Dame.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.288
I'm going from the airport
to the Hard Rock

00:12:37.288 --> 00:12:38.524
and back to the airport."

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:39.624
[ Laughter ]

00:12:39.624 --> 00:12:41.093
There aren't any --

00:12:41.093 --> 00:12:43.562
There's not a single
Sherlock Holmes novel called,

00:12:43.562 --> 00:12:45.897
"Sherlock Holmes And The
Actually That's Not Important,

00:12:45.897 --> 00:12:46.899
Don't Look at That."

00:12:46.899 --> 00:12:49.567
[ Laughter ]

00:12:49.567 --> 00:12:51.470
During the hearing last week,
Kavanaugh lied repeatedly

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.104
about key details
of his heavy-drinking

00:12:53.104 --> 00:12:55.007
high school and college days,
details that have been

00:12:55.007 --> 00:12:56.708
contradicted by many
of his classmates.

00:12:56.708 --> 00:12:59.577
Now, today, it is reported that
the White House told the FBI

00:12:59.577 --> 00:13:01.180
they can interview
anyone they deem necessary.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:02.615
And, of course, they should.

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:05.150
Not investigating Kavanaugh's
lies or interviewing people

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.118
who could corroborate
the allegations against him

00:13:07.118 --> 00:13:08.687
would be, in a word...

00:13:08.687 --> 00:13:09.722
-Loco.

00:13:09.722 --> 00:13:11.590
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:15.394
[ Cheers and applause ]

